@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] isolated-synthetic-secrets
Entrypoints MUST generate all database, TLS, signing, encryption and host credentials
at container startup into private runtime volumes. They MUST NOT print secret values,
put them in command arguments, or copy production credentials into images.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] truthful-readiness
Entrypoint health checks MUST require the real serving interface or reviewed
readiness socket. Marker files may only report completion of the specific
one-shot migration or enrollment action that created them.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] closed-fixture-inputs
Entrypoints MUST use fixed, validated synthetic host and storage identities and
the reviewed Marshall enrollment API. They MUST NOT insert enrollment rows or
fabricate physical capacity or Lilly readiness.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;verification] closed-control-operator
The enrollment operator MUST accept only exact private request schemas for its
named fixture actions. Host rotation MUST use Marshall's reviewed rotate and
verify CLI and publish an issued result only after verifying the private output
and reading committed host generation. Fixture actions MUST use their reviewed
Ash coordinators with a fresh stored synthetic login and real passkey assertion.
A failed or ambiguous operation MUST NOT be retried automatically or reported
as applied. Fixture bootstrap MUST mark its start durably before the first
account mutation; if it fails before manifest publication, restart MUST refuse
the partial fixture rather than silently create more credentials.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] enrollment-control-readiness
Enrollment health MUST be published only after the real lilly-a enrollment,
fixture publication and separate read-only workload credential copy complete.
The optional measured lilly-host enrollment MUST publish its own private host
fixture only after CLI credential verification and committed pool observation;
the inner host's health remains a separate gate. The operator process MUST
remain the enrollment container's main process so its failure terminates the
container.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery;security] enrico-fixed-release-restart
The Enrico container supervisor MUST accept only a private restart_enrico
request for its one immutable release child. It MUST confirm that child's
termination and new private health before issuing a result with distinct PIDs
and a higher durable launch generation. An interrupted or unconfirmed restart
MUST remain uncertain and MUST NOT be replayed automatically.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;security] enrico-passive-inode-observer
The Enrico observer MUST publish only the eight fixed native Git slot lock
identities, bounded UUID repository lock identities and their current
in-container /proc fd holders to a private read-only workload volume. It MUST
mark incomplete scans explicitly;
missing or stale evidence MUST NOT prove absence of descendants. It MUST NOT
accept a command, signal a process, or expose arguments or payload bytes.
